  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is an odd electron molecule so <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is paramagnetic<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0117_03bf5f560f00.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:0.99167in;height:0.84167in\" /><br />The dimer, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> , has no unpaired electron so it is diamagnetic.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0117_c72352d4db88.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.38333in;height:0.775in\" />"
